# This repository is a byte-for-byte project: the test suites compare generated
# output against committed golden files, and the parity gate diffs the Python and
# JavaScript cores down to the bytes of a ZIP archive. A line-ending translation
# anywhere in that chain is indistinguishable from a real regression.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every text file
# to CRLF on checkout. That is exactly what happened: all five windows-latest
# jobs failed with 29 mismatching goldens on a commit that changed no code.
#
# `-text` means: never translate, in either direction, on any platform. What is
# committed is what lands in the working tree.
* -text

# Fixture videos are binary; say so, so Git never tries to diff or merge them.
fixtures/bin/** binary
